op-input: a [[selection of titles|Title Selection]], each interpreted as a fragment of ~WikiText
op-output: the value of the first attribute named in <<.place A>> that is present in each input title
op-parameter: one or more attribute names
op-parameter-name: A
op-purpose: retrieve attribute values from widget, HTML element or macro invocations
tags: [[Filter Operators]] [[Special Operators]]
title: getattribute Operator
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

<<.from-version "5.5.0">> Each input title is parsed as inline ~WikiText. Unless it consists of exactly one widget, HTML element or macro invocation it is ignored; any whitespace either side of the invocation is permitted, but any other surrounding text is not.

The operands are attribute names, tried in order; the value of the first one that is present is appended to the output. Input titles for which none of the named attributes is present are ignored.

Because the input is parsed by ~TiddlyWiki itself, all of the equivalent ways of writing an invocation are recognised, and quoting is resolved for you:

|!Input |!`getattribute[$variable],[$name]` |!`getattribute[name],[0]` |
|`<<colour foreground>>` |`colour` |`foreground` |
|`<<colour name:foreground>>` |`colour` |`foreground` |
|`<<colour "tiddler-title-foreground">>` |`colour` |`tiddler-title-foreground` |
|`<$transclude $variable="colour" name="foreground"/>` |`colour` |`foreground` |
|`<$macrocall $name="colour" name="foreground"/>` |`colour` |`foreground` |

Note that:

* The parameters of a [[macro invocation|Macro Calls in WikiText]] are exposed as attributes. Positional parameters are named by their index, counting from zero, and the name of the macro itself is available as `$variable`
* Only attributes with a literal value are returned. Attributes whose value is computed &ndash; a [[filtered attribute value|Filtered Attribute Value]] `{{{ ... }}}`, an [[indirect attribute value|Indirect Attribute Value]] `{{ ... }}` or a macro attribute value `<< ... >>` &ndash; cannot be resolved without evaluating the invocation, and so are ignored

